Description: fast and privacy-focused web browser for Debian Linux
 Polecat Browser is a modern web browser built with Qt and Qt WebEngine.
 It provides tabbed browsing, multiple windows, bookmarks, history,
 a download manager, private browsing, privacy controls, content blocking
 and optional study tools in a clean, GNOME-inspired interface.
 .
 Polecat Browser contains no telemetry and no advertisements, and does not
 send browsing data to any remote service unless the user explicitly enables
 a feature that requires it.
 .
 It is built on Qt Widgets and Qt WebEngine, not on GNOME-specific libraries,
 so it runs unchanged across GNOME 48, 49 and 50 (and older releases) on both
 Wayland and X11 sessions. Installing the recommended qt6-wayland package gives
 a native Wayland session under recent GNOME.
